  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nOtt Based System Mini Reel — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow a user to create an account.\n2. The system shall enable a user to watch videos after they have created an account.\n3. The system shall permit a user to upload videos.\n4. The system shall allow a user to save videos in their likes list during video viewing.\n5. The system shall enable a user to view their saved videos from the likes list.\n6. The system shall allow a user to enter the discussion option.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\n- UserNotLoggedIn\n- UserLoggedOut\n- UserLoggedIn\n- UserUploadingVideo\n- UserViewingSavedVideos\n\nInitial state:\nUserNotLoggedIn\n\nFinal states:\nUserLoggedOut\n\nEvents or conditions:\n- CreateAccount\n- WatchVideos\n- UploadVideo\n- SaveVideo\n- ViewSavedVideos\n- EnterDiscussion\n\nTransitions:\n1. From UserNotLoggedIn to UserLoggedOut: CreateAccount\n2. From UserNotLoggedIn to UserLoggedIn: CreateAccount\n3. From UserLoggedOut to UserLoggedOut: WatchVideos, SaveVideo, ViewSavedVideos, EnterDiscussion\n4. From UserLoggedOut to UserLoggedOut: UploadVideo (invalid transition)\n5. From UserLoggedIn to UserLoggedOut: No specific event; user can log out manually\n6. From UserLoggedIn to UserUploadingVideo: UploadVideo\n7. From UserLoggedIn to UserViewingSavedVideos: ViewSavedVideos\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n- The requirement does not specify the conditions under which a user logs out, whether it